<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n106286" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑδᾰρής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδωρ</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>watery,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑδαρὲς διαχωρεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Prog.</u>
					11
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰχῶρες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					586b33
				</span></i>
			, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> mostly
			of wine, <i>mixed with too much water,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑδαρἦ ᾽νέχεέν σοι;—παντάπασι
					μὲν οὖν ὕδωρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pherecr.
					70
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
			</span></i>
			<i>Aër.</i><i><span class="en">
				9
			</span></i> (
				Sup.
			), <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Lac.</u>
				1.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.
				226
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				230
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				6.272
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεράννυται οὔθ᾽ ὑδαρὲς οὔτ᾽ ἄκρατον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antiph.
					24
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυλίκιον ὑ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					2
				</span></i>
			: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ χρύσιον κέρναν
				ὐδαρέστερον,</span> i.e. mix <i>with a higher proportion
				of alloy,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				12(2).1.14
			</span></i> (Mytil., <span class="entity">iv B. C.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> metaph., <i>washy, feeble, languid,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑδαρεῖ σαίνειν φιλότητι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					798
				</span></i>
			 (anap.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1262b15
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῦθος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Po.</u>
					1462b7
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. καὶ ψυχρὸς λόγος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					<u>Din.</u>
					11
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of colour,
				<i>watery, pale grey,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄμμα προβάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>GA</u>
					779a32
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> of taste,
				<i>insipid,</i> as plums, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				1.12.1
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
